# Licence of this project

**This project is distributed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or later
(AGPL-3.0-or-later), for as long as it uses the Swiss Ephemeris.**

## Why

The astrological calculations are done with the Swiss Ephemeris (through `pyswisseph`), by Astrodienst AG,
Zurich. The Swiss Ephemeris is dual-licensed (https://www.astro.com/swisseph/swephinfo_e.htm):

1. the **GNU Affero General Public License** - free of charge, but everything that links it must itself be
   AGPL, and users who interact with it **over a network** must be offered its complete source; or
2. the **Swiss Ephemeris Professional License** from Astrodienst AG - a one-time fee
   (https://www.astro.com/swisseph/swephprice_e.htm), which removes that obligation and is the normal
   choice for a closed-source commercial service.

We launch under option 1. That is a deliberate, temporary position:

- **The repository is public at launch and the deployed site offers its source.** `/about` carries the offer
  and the address of that repository (`SOURCE_URL` in the environment; see `app/web/site.py`). AGPL section 13
  asks for this, and a placeholder address is not an offer: `python -m app.hardening` **refuses to start the
  app in production** while `SOURCE_URL` still holds one, exactly as it refuses a missing `SESSION_SECRET`.
- **The position changes when the professional licence is bought.** It is bought within one week of the
  first real paid order. `app/payments/first_sale.py`
  records that moment (log at CRITICAL, `var/first_live_sale.json`, a row in the database);
  `scripts/first_sale_status.py` prints it. **From then on the source is no longer required to be published**:
  the repository may be made private and this notice, the `/about` section and the checklist item are updated
  together. Nothing else in the code depends on which licence is in force, and nothing that was already
  published under the AGPL can be un-published - that is what the licence granted to whoever took a copy.

## What is not ours

- **Swiss Ephemeris / pyswisseph** - Astrodienst AG, dual-licensed as above.
- **Noto Sans and Noto Sans Devanagari** (`app/pdf/fonts/`) - SIL Open Font License 1.1,
  `app/pdf/fonts/OFL.txt`. Embedding them in generated PDFs is expressly permitted.
- Everything else under `app/`, `scripts/`, `tests/` and `deploy/` is this project's own work.

The full text of the AGPL-3.0 is at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt.

> This file states which licence the project ships under and why. It is not legal advice: the choice between
> the two Swiss Ephemeris licences, and the wording of the source offer on the site, are worth a lawyer's
> five minutes before launch.
